                <pb facs="0484" n="398" sameAs="frus:frus1873p1v1/pg398"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.—Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">General Schenck to Mr.
                            Fish.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-07-01"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 1,
                        1873</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Respecting note to maritime powers, Lord Granville understands that Thornton not only read to you, but gave you a
                    copy of his instructions, and regards this as in usage equivalent to a written
                    answer by note.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
